    "title": "Preview and Design modes land in the in-app browser",
    "intro": "Today's nightly introduces a dedicated Preview/Design workflow for Aura's embedded browser, backed by a new CDP inspection path on the server, and follows up with a same-day polish pass to keep the toolbar usable at narrow widths.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-1",
        "time_label": "3:28 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-08-10T10:28:06.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-08-10T10:28:06.000Z",
        "title": "Preview and Design modes for the embedded browser",
        "summary": "A substantial interface and backend change adds two first-class modes to the in-app browser, with a new design toolbar, an element inspector, and Chromium/CDP-backed inspection plumbed from the Rust backend through to the UI.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Added Preview and Design modes to the browser panel, including a new BrowserDesignToolbar for switching modes and picking viewport presets (desktop, mobile, fit) and a BrowserDesignInspector surface for inspecting elements inside the page.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "fe5f7b0be4b01ffe678272ec42ce74463d8e53a3"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Extended the CDP backend with an inspect module and a new Inspect client message so the server can resolve elements by coordinates and stream InspectionResult events back over the browser WebSocket to the UI.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "fe5f7b0be4b01ffe678272ec42ce74463d8e53a3"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Turned on the Chromium/CDP browser backend for both the dev-channel and stable-channel server builds, so Preview and Design work in web-server deployments as well as the desktop package while feature-minimal builds can still fall back to the stub backend.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "fe5f7b0be4b01ffe678272ec42ce74463d8e53a3"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Reworked the browser viewport, panel, and input hooks around a shared design-context, and taught the agent chat panel about the new modes so agent interactions stay coherent when switching between Preview and Design.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "fe5f7b0be4b01ffe678272ec42ce74463d8e53a3"
            ],
            "confidence": "medium"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-2",
        "time_label": "5:58 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-08-10T12:58:17.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-08-10T12:58:17.000Z",
        "title": "Compact Preview toolbar no longer clips its controls",
        "summary": "A quick follow-up to the Preview/Design launch fixes layout clipping in narrow panels and makes the icon-only controls properly accessible.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Introduced a container query on the design toolbar so mode and viewport controls collapse to icon-only buttons under 360px and stop being clipped, with flex-shrink guards on the viewport group and divider to keep the layout stable.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "de66b3c2c2cb85b7ff460e020f8e9eeeac3db01a"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Added aria-label and title attributes to the Preview and Design buttons so the compact, icon-only state remains identifiable to screen readers and on hover, locked in by new regression tests for the toolbar.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "de66b3c2c2cb85b7ff460e020f8e9eeeac3db01a"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      }
